# Frontend

This is a student PWA used mostly on a phone. Desktop can look good, but mobile is the default.

## Layout

- Phone: bottom tab bar, not a sticky dark sidebar that turns into a horizontal scroller.
- Keep the 6 views: Dashboard, Attendance, Results, Materials, Resources, Settings.
- Respect safe-area insets. Main content must not hide under the tab bar.
- Touch targets at least 44px. Primary actions stay visible without hunting.

## Visual language

Reuse the existing tokens in `styles.css` (`--bg`, `--panel`, `--text`, `--muted`, `--line`, `--brand`). Do not invent a second palette.

Avoid AI-slop defaults:

- Giant display headings (`clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem)` and similar)
- Decorative "good / warn / bad" pills as the main UI
- 24px radius on every card, heavy drop shadows, Inter-everywhere dashboards
- Purple gradients, glassmorphism, blobs, fake empty-state illustrations
- 7-column calendars that overflow on a 360px screen

## Content density

- Dashboard should answer "am I in trouble?" in one screen, then get out of the way.
- Attendance calendar must be usable on a phone: compact cells or a list/week switch, not tiny unreadable day cards.
- Lists (materials, results) should scan: title, subject, one action. No nested card-in-card.

## How to change UI

Edit `index.html`, `styles.css`, and `app.js` only unless a new asset is required. Prefer CSS and markup changes over new JS frameworks.
